{"name":"Madera","hex":"#eed09d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Madera","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the county seat of Madera County, California, United States.","An unincorporated community in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Madera"}],"entries":[{"title":"Madera County, California","blocks":[{"text":"Madera County, officially the County of Madera, is a county located at the geographic center of the U.S. state of California. It features a varied landscape, encompassing the eastern San Joaquin Valley and the central Sierra Nevada, with Madera serving as the county seat. Established in 1893 from part of Fresno County, Madera County reported a population of 156,255 in the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg/330px-Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madera_County%2C_California","wikidata":"Q109661"},{"title":"Madera, California","blocks":[{"text":"Madera is a city in and the county seat of Madera County, located in the San Joaquin Valley of California. \nFounded in 1876 as a timber settlement at the terminus of a major log flume, the city grew around the lumber trade before transitioning to an agriculture-based economy during the 20th century. Irrigation from the San Joaquin River and nearby canals transformed the surrounding plains into fertile farmland that now supports vineyards, nut orchards, and row crops."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Madera%2C_California_-_Aerial_%2849394852076%29.jpg/330px-Madera%2C_California_-_Aerial_%2849394852076%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madera%2C_California","wikidata":"Q851000"}],"images":[{"srcset":"h